# Agent skills to reinstall on a fresh machine, one per line:
#
#     <source>  <name>
#
# `source` is whatever `skills add` accepts (a GitHub owner/repo, or a URL);
# `name` is the skill's directory name under ~/.agents/skills. Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored. `install.sh` walks this file and runs
# `npx skills add <source> -s <name> -g -y` for each entry.
#
# This replaces reading `.skill-lock.json`, which is no longer tracked. The
# lockfile is written by the skills CLI and rewrites `skillFolderHash` and
# `updatedAt` whenever a skill updates, so it showed up dirty in this repo
# constantly and blocked `ward repo refresh` -- while the only fields anything
# here ever read were the source and the name, which change only when you
# deliberately add or remove a skill. So: track the intent, ignore the state.
#
# The skill bodies themselves live untracked in ~/.agents/skills and are never
# committed.

crumley/intent-architecture  intent-architecture
vercel-labs/skills           find-skills
